{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"The file /Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/8f1a9339/tmp/msg.txt has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_012gvUVpyZaJPSgdZB9fn6zk","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"3eeeada3913c0c7857755d821b6c51542172b654","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","seq":505},"id":"ev1-b217b315cb7418d55b089c03a60e50b9f58954208fb24c7860c798aaf5d0b12f","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T05:03:08.827Z","producer":{"session_id":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.223","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"The file /Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/8f1a9339/tmp/msg.txt has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_012gvUVpyZaJPSgdZB9fn6zk","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"9e00b4c2-45f9-4672-b028-a16e26ad1729","promptId":"8fe54bff-ca64-4d3c-81d9-513f7a7381b1","sessionId":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9e00b4c2-45f9-4672-b028-a16e26ad1729","timestamp":"2026-08-06T05:03:08.827Z","toolUseResult":{"content":"gemini-cli: fix the dead sweep, the rewinding cursor, and the invisible snapshot drop\n\nThree defects found reviewing 0.20.0, all in the gemini-cli adapter, all\nverified against the real session file the adapter was built from.\n\nThe catch-up sweep never ran. It looked a cursor up by the session file's\nname, but capture wrote it under the sessionId declared inside the file --\n`session-2026-08-04T03-54-63ca4425` versus\n`63ca4425-bedf-43dc-8d39-a82310277fe9`, never equal for a real Gemini file.\nreadCursor returned null for every session, the sweep skipped every one of\nthem, and the gap-closing pass 0.19.0 added for claude-code was dead code\nhere. The cursor is now keyed by file name, which is the only identifier the\nsweep has before it reads anything; the session id events carry is unchanged.\nFree to fix now because gemini-cli is unreleased and no cursors exist yet.\n\nThe cursor could move backwards. Messages and mutations are walked in two\npasses and the second overwrote nextCursor with its own highest key, so a log\nending in messages left the cursor at the last metadata patch -- 1, on a\nfour-record file. Harmless (re-emitted records dedup) but it re-converted the\ntail on every hook fire forever. advance() is monotonic now.\n\nA snapshot that withdrew a message said nothing. The PR claimed a withdrawn\nturn was legible as withdrawn, but only `$rewindTo` produced an activity --\nand the incident that motivated the whole union-capture design was a\n`$set.messages` snapshot silently dropping a typed prompt, which produced\nonly a metadata patch with the messages stripped out. `rewound` was computed\nand never emitted. On the real session the recovered \"hi\" was\nindistinguishable from an ordinary turn. Snapshots now emit a `snapshot_drop`\nactivity naming the ids they removed, beside the existing `rewind`.\n\nAlso: those metadata events stored the entire conversation in `raw`, because\nGemini rewrites the whole message list into every `$set.messages`. On the\nfive-record real session the two snapshots were 22% of captured bytes, and\nthe share grows with conversation length. The message list is dropped from\nthe stored raw -- the one place an adapter prunes it -- since every message\nis already captured as its own event with its own verbatim raw.\n\nAnd `capture <gemini-cli|qwen-code> --all` now says which directory it looked\nin when it finds nothing, instead of reporting `+0 events` that reads as\n\"already captured\" when you are really one directory below the project root.\n\nTests: 200, 199 pass / 1 pre-existing skip. Three new gemini-cli tests cover\nthe cursor key and its monotonicity, the snapshot drop, and the raw pruning.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/8f1a9339/tmp/msg.txt","originalFile":"0.20.0: Gemini CLI and Qwen Code adapters\n\nAdds capture for the two CLIs at the top of the roadmap's TODO list, rebased\nonto 0.19.0 and built to its bar: no skip lists, every record gets a kind.\n\nGemini CLI (`~/.gemini/tmp/<project>/chats/session-*.jsonl`) is the harder of\nthe two: the file is append-only but is a write-ahead log of mutations to one\nconversation document, not a transcript. Capture replays it with Gemini's own\nrecord precedence, but deliberately does not honour its removals — verified on\na live session, Gemini rewrote the document after a failed API call and\nsilently dropped the prompt the user had just typed. The ledger keeps the\nunion of every message the file ever held, each at its last-written value, and\nrecords the `$rewindTo` itself as an `activity` naming what it withdrew, so a\nwithdrawn turn is legible as withdrawn rather than merely present. `$set`\npatches become `session_state`; `info`/`error`/`warning` notices become turns\nspoken by the system. Because nothing is removed, `seq` is assigned at first\nsighting over messages and mutations alike and never reused, so a rewind\ncannot renumber later turns. Sub-sessions under `<chats>/<parent id>/` are\ncaptured as sub-conversations.\n\nQwen Code (`~/.qwen/projects/<escaped-cwd>/chats/<id>.jsonl`) forked Gemini CLI\nbut not its store: plain append-only JSONL with a claude-code-shaped envelope,\nso the adapter is that adapter's twin — per-line conversion, line-index `seq`,\na torn-tail-safe cursor, the same catch-up sweep. Everything that is not a turn\narrives as a `system` line discriminated by `subtype`: `attribution_snapshot`\nbecomes `file_snapshot` (per-file content hashes are in the record itself, so\nnothing needs resolving against a local cache), the title/source/goal subtypes\nbecome `session_state`, `at_command` and the agent-launch prompts become\n`context_injection`, and everything else becomes `activity` rather than being\ndropped. A `parent_session` record makes a subagent chat a sub-conversation.\n\nBoth CLIs express content as Google GenAI `Part` lists, so that conversion is\nshared in genai-parts.ts.\n\nAlso:\n- Extracts the cursor into adapters/common.ts and puts all five adapters on\n  it. 0.19.0 taught the claude-code cursor three things the others still did\n  not know — absent is not zero, `size` bounds the sweep, the write must be\n  atomic — and the fix for each was worth having everywhere rather than in one\n  of five copies.\n- Fixes the torn-trailing-line bug in codex, which 0.19.0 fixed for\n  claude-code only: the cursor advanced past a half-written line, so the\n  completed line was never captured. Uses the same narrow rule (unterminated\n  file *and* final line), because holding at any parse failure would stall a\n  session's capture forever on real corruption.\n- `cledger capture <gemini-cli|qwen-code> --all` backfills every session the\n  CLI scopes to this directory; the hook's own sweep is deliberately narrower\n  and only finishes sessions cledger already tracks.\n\nVerified end to end against live CLIs: `cledger install qwen-code` followed by\na real `qwen` run captures the session automatically — 6 turns, 2 file\nsnapshots and 5 activity records, with the machinery kinds correctly hidden\nfrom the default `log` view.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc\n","structuredPatch":[{"lines":["-0.20.0: Gemini CLI and Qwen Code adapters","+gemini-cli: fix the dead sweep, the rewinding cursor, and the invisible snapshot drop"," ","-Adds capture for the two CLIs at the top of the roadmap's TODO list, rebased","-onto 0.19.0 and built to its bar: no skip lists, every record gets a kind.","+Three defects found reviewing 0.20.0, all in the gemini-cli adapter, all","+verified against the real session file the adapter was built from."," ","-Gemini CLI (`~/.gemini/tmp/<project>/chats/session-*.jsonl`) is the harder of","-the two: the file is append-only but is a write-ahead log of mutations to one","-conversation document, not a transcript. Capture replays it with Gemini's own","-record precedence, but deliberately does not honour its removals — verified on","-a live session, Gemini rewrote the document after a failed API call and","-silently dropped the prompt the user had just typed. The ledger keeps the","-union of every message the file ever held, each at its last-written value, and","-records the `$rewindTo` itself as an `activity` naming what it withdrew, so a","-withdrawn turn is legible as withdrawn rather than merely present. `$set`","-patches become `session_state`; `info`/`error`/`warning` notices become turns","-spoken by the system. Because nothing is removed, `seq` is assigned at first","-sighting over messages and mutations alike and never reused, so a rewind","-cannot renumber later turns. Sub-sessions under `<chats>/<parent id>/` are","-captured as sub-conversations.","+The catch-up sweep never ran. It looked a cursor up by the session file's","+name, but capture wrote it under the sessionId declared inside the file --","+`session-2026-08-04T03-54-63ca4425` versus","+`63ca4425-bedf-43dc-8d39-a82310277fe9`, never equal for a real Gemini file.","+readCursor returned null for every session, the sweep skipped every one of","+them, and the gap-closing pass 0.19.0 added for claude-code was dead code","+here. The cursor is now keyed by file name, which is the only identifier the","+sweep has before it reads anything; the session id events carry is unchanged.","+Free to fix now because gemini-cli is unreleased and no cursors exist yet."," ","-Qwen Code (`~/.qwen/projects/<escaped-cwd>/chats/<id>.jsonl`) forked Gemini CLI","-but not its store: plain append-only JSONL with a claude-code-shaped envelope,","-so the adapter is that adapter's twin — per-line conversion, line-index `seq`,","-a torn-tail-safe cursor, the same catch-up sweep. Everything that is not a turn","-arrives as a `system` line discriminated by `subtype`: `attribution_snapshot`","-becomes `file_snapshot` (per-file content hashes are in the record itself, so","-nothing needs resolving against a local cache), the title/source/goal subtypes","-become `session_state`, `at_command` and the agent-launch prompts become","-`context_injection`, and everything else becomes `activity` rather than being","-dropped. A `parent_session` record makes a subagent chat a sub-conversation.","+The cursor could move backwards. Messages and mutations are walked in two","+passes and the second overwrote nextCursor with its own highest key, so a log","+ending in messages left the cursor at the last metadata patch -- 1, on a","+four-record file. Harmless (re-emitted records dedup) but it re-converted the","+tail on every hook fire forever. advance() is monotonic now."," ","-Both CLIs express content as Google GenAI `Part` lists, so that conversion is","-shared in genai-parts.ts.","+A snapshot that withdrew a message said nothing. The PR claimed a withdrawn","+turn was legible as withdrawn, but only `$rewindTo` produced an activity --","+and the incident that motivated the whole union-capture design was a","+`$set.messages` snapshot silently dropping a typed prompt, which produced","+only a metadata patch with the messages stripped out. `rewound` was computed","+and never emitted. On the real session the recovered \"hi\" was","+indistinguishable from an ordinary turn. Snapshots now emit a `snapshot_drop`","+activity naming the ids they removed, beside the existing `rewind`."," ","-Also:","-- Extracts the cursor into adapters/common.ts and puts all five adapters on","-  it. 0.19.0 taught the claude-code cursor three things the others still did","-  not know — absent is not zero, `size` bounds the sweep, the write must be","-  atomic — and the fix for each was worth having everywhere rather than in one","-  of five copies.","-- Fixes the torn-trailing-line bug in codex, which 0.19.0 fixed for","-  claude-code only: the cursor advanced past a half-written line, so the","-  completed line was never captured. Uses the same narrow rule (unterminated","-  file *and* final line), because holding at any parse failure would stall a","-  session's capture forever on real corruption.","-- `cledger capture <gemini-cli|qwen-code> --all` backfills every session the","-  CLI scopes to this directory; the hook's own sweep is deliberately narrower","-  and only finishes sessions cledger already tracks.","+Also: those metadata events stored the entire conversation in `raw`, because","+Gemini rewrites the whole message list into every `$set.messages`. On the","+five-record real session the two snapshots were 22% of captured bytes, and","+the share grows with conversation length. The message list is dropped from","+the stored raw -- the one place an adapter prunes it -- since every message","+is already captured as its own event with its own verbatim raw."," ","-Verified end to end against live CLIs: `cledger install qwen-code` followed by","-a real `qwen` run captures the session automatically — 6 turns, 2 file","-snapshots and 5 activity records, with the machinery kinds correctly hidden","-from the default `log` view.","+And `capture <gemini-cli|qwen-code> --all` now says which directory it looked","+in when it finds nothing, instead of reporting `+0 events` that reads as","+\"already captured\" when you are really one directory below the project root."," ","+Tests: 200, 199 pass / 1 pre-existing skip. Three new gemini-cli tests cover","+the cursor key and its monotonicity, the snapshot drop, and the raw pruning.","+"," Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>"," Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc"],"newLines":46,"newStart":1,"oldLines":56,"oldStart":1}],"type":"update","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"d2c13890-188c-430b-9481-bd93ed6a94dd","version":"2.1.223"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-06T05:05:25.648Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
