{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"I've finished the review. Here's what I found.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Not finished — two real bugs, one of which makes a headline feature not actually do what the PR says.** The core of the work is solid: I verified the Gemini replay logic line-by-line against `loadConversationRecord` in the shipped `@google/gemini-cli@0.53.1` bundle (record precedence, `$rewindTo` inclusive-removal, unknown-target-clears-all, `$set.messages` replace, upsert-by-id) and it matches exactly, including the predicates. Qwen's `RECORD_TYPES` and `KNOWN_RECORD_SUBTYPES` are quoted correctly from `@qwen-code/qwen-code@0.21.5`. Build + 197 tests pass (196/1 pre-existing skip). Running both adapters over your real local session files produced 131 qwen events and 6 gemini events with **zero drift warnings**.\n\n## Bugs\n\n**1. The Gemini catch-up sweep never runs. Dead code.** `src/adapters/gemini-cli.ts:858`\n\nThe sweep looks up the cursor under the *filename stem*, but capture writes it under the *declared `sessionId`*. Those are never the same for a real Gemini file. Confirmed against your actual session:\n\n```\nsweep looks up cursor named   : session-2026-08-04T03-54-63ca4425.json\ncursor files actually on disk : [ '63ca4425-bedf-43dc-8d39-a82310277fe9.json' ]\n```\n\n`readCursor` returns null → `continue` → nothing is ever swept. Primary capture still works (I confirmed Gemini's `createBaseInput` always supplies `transcript_path`), so this is a lost safety net rather than lost capture — but it's exactly the gap 0.19.0 shipped to close for claude-code. Zero test coverage: `runGeminiHook`, `sweepStaleSessions`, and `captureGeminiAll` are untested.\n\nThe clean fix is to key Gemini cursors by filename stem like the other four adapters. That resets existing cursors — which costs nothing *right now* because gemini-cli is new in this PR and no cursors exist in the wild yet. It gets expensive after you ship.\n\n**2. The Gemini cursor moves backwards.** `src/adapters/gemini-cli.ts:675-676`\n\nThe mutation loop runs after the message loop and overwrites `nextCursor` with `lastMutationSeq + 1`. On a 4-record file (seqs 0–3) the cursor is written as **1**:\n\n```\nfirst capture:  +4 events → cursor {\"messages\":1,...}\nsecond capture: +0 events (3 deduped) → cursor {\"messages\":4,...}\n```\n\nNo data loss (dedup catches it) but every hook fire redoes the tail. `Math.max` fixes it.\n\n## The intent mismatch — and it's the important one\n\n**The motivating case is not actually made legible.** The PR body and README both say a withdrawn turn is \"legible as withdrawn rather than merely present,\" citing the incident where Gemini dropped your typed prompt after a failed API call. But that loss happened via a **`$set.messages` snapshot truncation**, not a `$rewindTo`. The adapter emits an `activity` for `$rewindTo` only. A snapshot truncation produces just a `session_state/metadata` event with `messages` stripped out by `patchFields`.\n\n`session.rewound` is computed at `gemini-cli.ts:300` and used only to break the settledness hold at line 648 — it is **never emitted**. On your real captured session the recovered prompt looks like this:\n\n```\nseq=3 conversation_turn actor=human :: hi\n```\n\nIndistinguishable from an ordinary turn. The union-capture half works and is genuinely valuable; the legibility half only covers the path that didn't happen to you.\n\n## Smaller notes\n\n- Qwen `convertLine` silently drops a `user`/`assistant`/`tool_result` line with no `timestamp` — no drift record, no preservation. This matches claude-code's existing convention (`claude-code.ts:479`), so it's a shared pre-existing gap rather than a regression, but it sits oddly against 0.19.0's \"no skip lists\" bar.\n- `capture <source> --all` silently reports `+0 events` if cwd isn't the exact registered project root (subdirectory, or a worktree). Consistent with the other adapters, but silent-zero is an easy way to think capture is broken.\n- `sessionIdFromPath`'s doc comment claims it extracts the id embedded in `session-<ts>-<id>.jsonl`; it returns the whole stem. That wrong comment is arguably what hid bug #1.\n\n## Yes, it needs a manual TUI smoke test — and more than you'd think\n\nYour real Gemini session contains **one human turn, one system-context turn, and four metadata patches. Zero model turns.** So essentially the whole Gemini conversion path has only synthetic unit-test coverage: `modelBlocks` (including the `callsInContent`/`thoughtsInContent` precedence branch that prevents double-emitting tool calls), the `isSettled` withhold-and-hold-cursor logic, `thoughts`, `toolCalls` result appending, the `info`/`error`/`warning` notice path, the rewind activity, and the subagent directory scan.\n\nWorth driving by hand:\n\n1. **Gemini, interactive, with tool calls** — the single highest-value test. Confirms `modelBlocks` precedence and that a mid-flight turn is withheld at `AfterAgent` then picked up at `SessionEnd` rather than frozen half-finished.\n2. **Gemini `/rewind`** — the one path where the rewind `activity` actually fires.\n3. **Gemini interactive at all** — the `>/dev/null 2>&1` detach was verified on Qwen 0.21.5 only; the install applies it to Gemini too, and `AfterAgent` only fires in a live TUI.\n4. **Qwen: a subagent, an `@file` reference, `/chat save <title>`** — `parent_session`, `at_command`, and `custom_title` are all mapped from Qwen's source list, never from a transcript. Your 19 local sessions contain only `user`/`assistant`/`tool_result`/`ui_telemetry`/`attribution_snapshot`.\n5. **Gemini's sweep** — untestable until bug #1 is fixed.\n\nOne thing to decide rather than fix: 57 of 131 qwen events are `ui_telemetry` activity records. That's the 0.19.0 capture-everything bar working as designed, but it means telemetry outnumbers content in the ledger.\n\nWant me to fix the two bugs and close the rewind/snapshot legibility gap? All three are small and localized.\n\nresult:\nPR #5 is not finished — Gemini's catch-up sweep is dead code (cursor key mismatch, confirmed empirically), its cursor rewinds each capture, and the \"withdrawn turns are legible\" claim only covers `$rewindTo` while the real-world loss it cites came from `$set.messages` truncation, which emits no record; format claims verified correct against both CLIs' shipped sources, and manual TUI smoke tests are needed since no real Gemini model turn has ever been captured.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"3eeeada3913c0c7857755d821b6c51542172b654","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","seq":342},"id":"ev1-91b2d159304b7cbeff722ebf37b6d20f879c2d7bb2fa2adc7f960f9766c97500","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T04:47:43.025Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.223","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"I've finished the review. Here's what I found.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Not finished — two real bugs, one of which makes a headline feature not actually do what the PR says.** The core of the work is solid: I verified the Gemini replay logic line-by-line against `loadConversationRecord` in the shipped `@google/gemini-cli@0.53.1` bundle (record precedence, `$rewindTo` inclusive-removal, unknown-target-clears-all, `$set.messages` replace, upsert-by-id) and it matches exactly, including the predicates. Qwen's `RECORD_TYPES` and `KNOWN_RECORD_SUBTYPES` are quoted cor