hhold-and-hold-cursor logic, `thoughts`, `toolCalls` result appending, the `info`/`error`/`warning` notice path, the rewind activity, and the subagent directory scan.\n\nWorth driving by hand:\n\n1. **Gemini, interactive, with tool calls** — the single highest-value test. Confirms `modelBlocks` precedence and that a mid-flight turn is withheld at `AfterAgent` then picked up at `SessionEnd` rather than frozen half-finished.\n2. **Gemini `/rewind`** — the one path where the rewind `activity` actually fires.\n3. **Gemini interactive at all** — the `>/dev/null 2>&1` detach was verified on Qwen 0.21.5 only; the install applies it to Gemini too, and `AfterAgent` only fires in a live TUI.\n4. **Qwen: a subagent, an `@file` reference, `/chat save <title>`** — `parent_session`, `at_command`, and `custom_title` are all mapped from Qwen's source list, never from a transcript. Your 19 local sessions contain only `user`/`assistant`/`tool_result`/`ui_telemetry`/`attribution_snapshot`.\n5. **Gemini's sweep** — untestable until bug #1 is fixed.\n\nOne thing to decide rather than fix: 57 of 131 qwen events are `ui_telemetry` activity records. That's the 0.19.0 capture-everything bar working as designed, but it means telemetry outnumbers content in the ledger.\n\nWant me to fix the two bugs and close the rewind/snapshot legibility gap? All three are small and localized.\n\nresult:\nPR #5 is not finished — Gemini's catch-up sweep is dead code (cursor key mismatch, confirmed empirically), its cursor rewinds each capture, and the \"withdrawn turns are legible\" claim only covers `$rewindTo` while the real-world loss it cites came from `$set.messages` truncation, which emits no record; format claims verified correct against both CLIs' shipped sources, and manual TUI smoke tests are needed since no real Gemini model turn has ever been captured.","type":"text"}],"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011CdktTqpsucDQyui1ByXD3","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reaso